(968385, 113200, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like the colors. I would suggest that it might have been better to crop it so that the title of the book doesn''t show. It''s not a particularly significant title and the white lettering at the bottom is a bit distracting. The lighting is a tad flat -- although the exposure looks good I''d like to see a bit more rounding of form on the apple with a slightly darker shadow area falling on the book for a bit of depth.</td>', 'I like the colors. I would suggest that it might have been better to crop it so that the title of the book doesn''t show. It''s not a particularly significant title and the white lettering at the bottom is a bit distracting. The lighting is a tad flat -- although the exposure looks good I''d like to see a bit more rounding of form on the apple with a slightly darker shadow area falling on the book for a bit of depth.', '2004-10-21 12:53:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(968386, 113839, 7322, '<td valign="top">Nikce lighiting and good still-life set-up. The black and white looks a bit cold to me. I suggest warming it up a bit by adjusting the Red in the RGB Levels.</td>', 'Nikce lighiting and good still-life set-up. The black and white looks a bit cold to me. I suggest warming it up a bit by adjusting the Red in the RGB Levels.', '2004-10-21 12:54:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(968390, 113919, 7322, '<td valign="top">Angus Young? Disturbing. LOL!<br/>It''s a funny set-up but it looks a bit snapshot-y to me. The flash lighting is flat and dull and the red-eye and glare on the glasses gives the photo an amateurish quality. To avoid glare on eyeglasses (or windows, etc), particularly when using a flash, try shooting at a slight angle.</td>', 'Angus Young? Disturbing. LOL!It''s a funny set-up but it looks a bit snapshot-y to me. The flash lighting is flat and dull and the red-eye and glare on the glasses gives the photo an amateurish quality. To avoid glare on eyeglasses (or windows, etc), particularly when using a flash, try shooting at a slight angle.', '2004-10-21 12:59:09.000000', NULL, 1),
