(975961, 113837, 25150, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!!<br/>let me start by saying it''s a great idea, but there is some strange stuff going on in the forground of the image. It looks as if you shot this photo though a glass? Is that frost that is softening the focus on the right and left of the photo? I also find the bottom crop a little distracting. If the bottom was cropped a little tighter, it wouldn''t feel so "unbalanced" especially since this is such a "balanced" shot.<br/> <br/>I understand why you chose BW, but I really think it would have worked much better in color. The sharpness in the center pencils is good, but I really think this scored as low as it did because of the distracting blur in the forground. I think that one aspect alone dropped your score. <br/> <br/>Overall, it''s a great idea, and a nice shot!<br/>Keep it up, clean it up, and you should be scoring higher in the future :)<br/>E</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!!!let me start by saying it''s a great idea, but there is some strange stuff going on in the forground of the image. It looks as if you shot this photo though a glass? Is that frost that is softening the focus on the right and left of the photo? I also find the bottom crop a little distracting. If the bottom was cropped a little tighter, it wouldn''t feel so "unbalanced" especially since this is such a "balanced" shot. I understand why you chose BW, but I really think it would have worked much better in color. The sharpness in the center pencils is good, but I really think this scored as low as it did because of the distracting blur in the forground. I think that one aspect alone dropped your score.  Overall, it''s a great idea, and a nice shot!Keep it up, clean it up, and you should be scoring higher in the future :)E', '2004-10-27 10:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
