(1057675, 113767, 6900, '<td valign="top">Annyong haseo!  I spent a year in Korea myself, teaching kids just like this one!  It''s a beautiful country.  This shot really takes me back.  I have a folder full of my kids.  What was his English name?  :)  They all seem to have them.  (I named a kid "Marx" once. Funny cuz I meant Groucho and he spent a weekend researching Karl.<br/> <br/>The picture is slightly out of focus, but that doesn''t detract from the image.  He''s focusing hard enough!  I don''t like the reallllly light blue shirt distracting from his face tho - his concentration is key and I would burn the shirt a little to darken it enough that it didn''t distract me.<br/> <br/>M</td>', 'Annyong haseo!  I spent a year in Korea myself, teaching kids just like this one!  It''s a beautiful country.  This shot really takes me back.  I have a folder full of my kids.  What was his English name?  :)  They all seem to have them.  (I named a kid "Marx" once. Funny cuz I meant Groucho and he spent a weekend researching Karl. The picture is slightly out of focus, but that doesn''t detract from the image.  He''s focusing hard enough!  I don''t like the reallllly light blue shirt distracting from his face tho - his concentration is key and I would burn the shirt a little to darken it enough that it didn''t distract me. M', '2004-12-11 20:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1057700, 113767, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very satisfying image to look at. Certainly in the candid genre. What is most appealing is the universal pose. We have all been there and we truly sympathise with the subject. Well, in one slice of time you have no doubt captured the character, the internal sweet agony and elevated the package to a wonderful portrait exemplifying the battle between interest and apathy. But heck, the mountain is not really that high, it just appears so. Eventually we grow and conquer.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-11 21:23:28.</i></td>', 'A very satisfying image to look at. Certainly in the candid genre. What is most appealing is the universal pose. We have all been there and we truly sympathise with the subject. Well, in one slice of time you have no doubt captured the character, the internal sweet agony and elevated the package to a wonderful portrait exemplifying the battle between interest and apathy. But heck, the mountain is not really that high, it just appears so. Eventually we grow and conquer.', '2004-12-11 21:21:50.000000', '2004-12-11 21:23:28.000000', 0),
(1064919, 114032, 17507, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nephrotic:</b></div><hr/><i> There seemed to be a lack of black. I put it into photoshop and moved the sliders around - it makes a huge difference. I would be happy to email my changes and see what you feel. Definately has commercial potential </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think he''s right - if the contrast were better, this would work much better. The value range is skewed towards the greys and whites, which results in a washed-out looking image. Especially where soft focus shots are concerned, having good value is important.</td>', 'Originally posted by nephrotic: There seemed to be a lack of black. I put it into photoshop and moved the sliders around - it makes a huge difference. I would be happy to email my changes and see what you feel. Definately has commercial potential   I think he''s right - if the contrast were better, this would work much better. The value range is skewed towards the greys and whites, which results in a washed-out looking image. Especially where soft focus shots are concerned, having good value is important.', '2004-12-15 20:53:40.000000', NULL, 0),
